I'd like to reintroduce an old game that we've had on the SDF Public Access 
UNIX system for about 16 years now.  Its called MDG - Multiplayer Dungeon Game
and its basically a cross between rogue/nethack and a mud.  Players can 
quest partnered, in groups or alone and face various monsters from the common
Anhkheg to the fierce White Dragon.  While the game has a hack -n- slash
feel, it also deals heavily in magic with all characters having the ability
to study and cast spells.  The multi-player/chat feature is not the only 'mud 
like' aspect to the game.  One of the objects of the game is to quest deep
into the dungeons to collect Crystals (shown as Crystal Powers) which allow
players to interactively 'edit' each area.

If you are interested in playing this game, it requires shell access on SDF
(which is available instantly and freely) by telnetting to 'sdf.lonestar.org'
and logging on as 'new'.  The game itself runs on a dedicated node, so once
you have created your account, you'll have to login to that node specifically
and then type 'mdg' to join the game.  Once your account has been created
you can use SSH to connect.  Also, you are encouraged to 'man mdg' from your
shell account to learn more about mdg!  Please feel free to email me if you
have any problems or have questions.

Here are a few 'screen shots' and descriptions of what game play is like.

I.  Here kthorn, Hectic Elf and myrddin are questing in an underwater
    cave.  The '[' is a shield left on the ground.  '$' is gold.  '>' is a
    stairwell going down.  (more info in 'man mdg').  Players move 
    around the sector/area using 'vi' keys h,j,k,l with y/u & b/n for
    diagonal movement.  The players are all partners so they won't
    kill each other.  2> (kthorn) instructs the other players to 
    wait for him to enter the cave first.

